    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "97ce23f4-3d14-31ef-b9e9-5edfe4cbc611",
                "word": "unprovided",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "df41d365-09fa-38d1-a440-ef5635c857ae",
                        "entry_id": "97ce23f4-3d14-31ef-b9e9-5edfe4cbc611",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Not provided; not supplied or equipped; unprepared."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d0854d93-52d7-4f9f-ba26-1b2d66cc500b",
                                "sense_id": "df41d365-09fa-38d1-a440-ef5635c857ae",
                                "text": "The shepheards God so wel them guided,\nThat of nought they were unprovided,\nButter enough, honye, milke, and whay,\nAnd their flockes fleeces, them to araye."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5408f33d-d144-4b4e-a8e5-b9ee0679c837",
                                "sense_id": "df41d365-09fa-38d1-a440-ef5635c857ae",
                                "text": "Why, sir, you know this is your wedding-day.\nFirst were we sad, fearing you would not come;\nNow sadder, that you come so unprovided.\nFie, doff this habit, shame to your estate,\nAn eye-sore to our solemn festival!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6aa5efeb-712a-46f3-a7ef-3d51ba1b6f87",
                                "sense_id": "df41d365-09fa-38d1-a440-ef5635c857ae",
                                "text": "Mean while, if you are unprovided of a Lodging, I dare undertake, you shall be welcome to this Gentlewoman."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "91aaf765-8dac-4849-8d29-7f6191afeca6",
                                "sense_id": "df41d365-09fa-38d1-a440-ef5635c857ae",
                                "text": "Miss Tilney, understanding in part her friend’s curiosity to see the house, soon revived the subject; and her father being, contrary to Catherine’s expectations, unprovided with any pretence for further delay […] was at last ready to escort them."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4e5e3816-5c4c-477a-8a0c-e61c0e1eb4f3",
                                "sense_id": "df41d365-09fa-38d1-a440-ef5635c857ae",
                                "text": "Perhaps it is an oversight on Mr Macgregor’s part that he has left these young infants quite unprovided for, and that some of their mothers are in danger of starvation […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4f118bfc-f81f-4d4f-8092-10fda12ae8e9",
                                "sense_id": "df41d365-09fa-38d1-a440-ef5635c857ae",
                                "text": "Originally unprovided with cabs, the first to acquire them did so during the Webb period in the 1890's, [...]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "50cb219c-f49a-4744-aed1-88a4b18a7d19",
                                "sense_id": "df41d365-09fa-38d1-a440-ef5635c857ae",
                                "text": "[...] but there are other northbound trains, unprovided with any refreshments, on which this car's appearance would be most welcome, [...]."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
